WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:05.720
Without a ribber,
knitting ribbing with knit purl stitches

00:00:05.753 --> 00:00:09.170
on a flatbed machine
takes quite a bit of work.

00:00:09.203 --> 00:00:15.240
You need to reform individual
stitches to create the ribbing.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.680
Now, there's no law that says you can't
include hand knitting with your machine

00:00:32.713 --> 00:00:35.170
knitting to obtain the look you want.

00:00:35.203 --> 00:00:38.760
Even if you have a ribber,
sometimes it's faster and easier just

00:00:38.793 --> 00:00:42.600
to pull out your needles,
cast on, and knit a bit of ribbing,

00:00:42.633 --> 00:00:45.810
and hang it back on the machine,
and off you go.

00:00:45.843 --> 00:00:49.530
The trick is to select the size
of the hand knitting needles that's

00:00:49.563 --> 00:00:52.920
appropriate for the yarn you're using.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.120
If you're using hand
knitting yarn, it's easy.

00:00:59.153 --> 00:01:02.130
Just use the yarn label as a guide.

00:01:02.163 --> 00:01:05.920
Now, if you're using cone yarn,
here's a general guideline based

00:01:05.953 --> 00:01:09.130
on the pitch of your machine.

00:01:09.163 --> 00:01:14.210
At first, it'll take a little bit of trial
and error, but with experience,

00:01:14.243 --> 00:01:17.960
you'll learn what needles to use.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.560
4.5 millimeter machines or standard gauge,
you'll probably use

00:01:22.593 --> 00:01:26.650
a size 1 to 3 US needle.

00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:32.210
On mid gauge machines, you'll use
somewhere between a 4 and a 6.

00:01:32.243 --> 00:01:39.120
On 9 millimeter machines,
you'll use a US size 7 to 9.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.360
Now, when you hang your ribbing
on the machine, you need to keep in mind

00:01:44.393 --> 00:01:50.250
the public or the right side of both
the knitting and your garment fabric.

00:01:50.283 --> 00:01:55.770
Some ribbing or cast on, knitting cast on,
have a right and a wrong side.

00:01:55.803 --> 00:02:00.730
So you need to really think about
the right side of your ribbing

00:02:00.763 --> 00:02:05.000
and which side of the garment fabric
you're going to be using for the right

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:08.570
side so that when you take the piece off
the machine,

00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:11.930
you've got the public side showing.

00:02:11.963 --> 00:02:16.040
I suggest you take a time
to try this technique.

00:02:16.073 --> 00:02:20.530
Just knit a little ribbon on some hand
knitting needles, hang it on the machine,

00:02:20.563 --> 00:02:22.890
and see how easy it is.

00:02:22.923 --> 00:02:28.327
It'll probably open a wide range
of possibilities for you in using hand

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.200
knitting along with your machine knitting.


